#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# trig_to_exp

#% text
# `trig_to_exp(e)` writes trigonometric and hyperbolic functions as exponentials.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `sin(x)` becomes `(exp(im*x) - exp(-im*x))/(2*im)`, `cosh(x)` becomes `(exp(x) + exp(-x))/2`, and the other functions are quotients of these.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
trig_to_exp(sin(x))
#% output
#= -im/2*exp(im*x) + (im/2)*exp(-im*x)

#% cell
trig_to_exp(cos(x))
#% output
#= (1/2)*exp(-im*x) + (1/2)*exp(im*x)

#% cell
trig_to_exp(cosh(x))
#% output
#= (1/2)*exp(x) + (1/2)*exp(-x)

#% cell
trig_to_exp(tanh(x))
#% output
#= exp(x)/(exp(x) + exp(-x)) - exp(-x)/(exp(x) + exp(-x))

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# A trigonometric identity, checked through exponentials:

#% cell
expand(trig_to_exp(sin(x)^2 + cos(x)^2))
#% output
#= 1

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `exp_to_trig` goes the other way:

#% cell
exp_to_trig(trig_to_exp(sin(x)))
#% output
#= sin(x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `exp_to_trig`, `trig_expand`, `exp`
